{"name": "cvaos", "game": "Castlevania - Aria of Sorrow", "version": "2026.6.22", "hidden": false, "groups": [{"name": "Game Options", "options": [{"name": "progression_balancing", "display_name": "Progression Balancing", "description": "A system that can move progression earlier, to try and prevent the player from getting stuck and bored early.\n\nA lower setting means more getting stuck. A higher setting means less getting stuck.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "NamedRange", "default": 50, "min": 0, "max": 99, "presets": {"disabled": 0, "normal": 50, "extreme": 99}}, {"name": "accessibility", "display_name": "Accessibility", "description": "Set rules for reachability of your items/locations.\n\n**Full:** ensure everything can be reached and acquired.\n\n**Minimal:** ensure what is needed to reach your goal can be acquired.\n\n**Items:** ensure all logically relevant items can be acquired. Some items, such as keys, may be self-locking, and\nsome locations may be inaccessible.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Choice", "default": 1, "choices": [{"name": "full", "display_name": "Full", "value": 0}, {"name": "minimal", "display_name": "Minimal", "value": 2}, {"name": "items", "display_name": "Items", "value": 1}]}, {"name": "randomize_pickups", "display_name": "Randomize Pickups", "description": "Adds the one-time on-the-ground pickups to the randomization pool.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Toggle", "default": true}, {"name": "goal", "display_name": "Goal", "description": "The win condition.\n\n- chaos: defeat Chaos form two.\n- graham: defeat Graham (with any equipment).", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Choice", "default": 0, "choices": [{"name": "chaos", "display_name": "Chaos", "value": 0}, {"name": "graham", "display_name": "Graham", "value": 1}]}, {"name": "hard_mode", "display_name": "Hard Mode", "description": "Turns on Hard Mode (the client forces the relevant nibble).\n\nShuffles the game's Hard Mode pickups (Kaiser Knuckle, Death's Sickle, Death's Robe,\n   Silver Gun, Tear of Blood). The game only spawns those five in Hard Mode, so when this is\n   off they are excluded from the location pool and item pool entirely.\n\nMakes enemies take less damage.\n\nOstensibly makes unearned souls easier to obtain.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Toggle", "default": false}, {"name": "skull_key_warp", "display_name": "Skull Key Warp", "description": "Turns the Skull Key into a warp item: using it from the Consumables menu teleports Soma to the\n   starting room.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Toggle", "default": true}, {"name": "death_link", "display_name": "Death Link", "description": "When you die, everyone who enabled death link dies. Of course, the reverse is true too.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Toggle", "default": false}], "collapsed": false}, {"name": "Item Smoothing", "options": [{"name": "item_smoothing", "display_name": "Item Smoothing", "description": "**This is the flag to turn off if you want a totally-random-yet-finishable run.**\n\nBiases item placement so less-desirable items show up earlier and more-desirable ones later,\n   using community tier-list data (data/item_balancing). Progression items are never moved by\n   this; the three Ancient Books are spread across early/mid/late instead of treated as junk.\n\n- off: vanilla placement -- any item can appear anywhere.\n- loose: gentle escalation with wide, long-tailed luck (more surprises, lucky early finds).\n- strict: stronger escalation with tighter placement (fewer surprises).", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Choice", "default": 2, "choices": [{"name": "off", "display_name": "Off", "value": 0}, {"name": "loose", "display_name": "Loose", "value": 1}, {"name": "strict", "display_name": "Strict", "value": 2}]}, {"name": "item_smoothing_order", "display_name": "Item Smoothing Order", "description": "No effect when Item Smoothing is off.\n\nExplanation:\n\nWhen Item Smoothing is on:\n    option_spheres = good stuff generally appears later in the run\n    option_map_distance = good stuff generally appears in later original-game spots\n\nFor example: does Claimh Solais (a very strong weapon) show up later in the run (spheres),\n    or in a spot that would be accessed late in the original game (map_distance)?\n\n\nWe default to \"option_map_distance\" to make sure you can find good stuff if forced into a \n    hard area.\n\nNote that this does not affect progression item placement, which is handled separately.\n\nOptions:\n\n- spheres: logical reachability order, measured after randomization -- how deep into *this\n  seed's* progression a location actually sits. Seed-specific.\n- map_distance: structural distance from the start in the unrandomized map (the region graph),\n  ignoring access rules and randomization. Seed-independent: a room is always \"as early\"\n  regardless of where progression landed.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Choice", "default": 1, "choices": [{"name": "spheres", "display_name": "Spheres", "value": 0}, {"name": "map_distance", "display_name": "Map Distance", "value": 1}]}, {"name": "early_mobility_souls", "display_name": "Early Mobility Souls", "description": "No effect when Item Smoothing is off.\n\nWhen Item Smoothing is on, how the three vertical mobility souls (Malphas/DJump, Hippogryph, and\n   Giant bat) are placed. They gate movement, so this is a separate axis from item desirability.\n\n- off: no special handling -- the souls place like any other progression item.\n- bias_early: ~93% of seeds pull one mobility soul (usually double jump) into the first third of\n  the run, while the heavier flight souls stay late; the rest leave all three late.\n- guarantee_early: always pull one mobility soul early, so you never start fully mobility-starved.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Choice", "default": 1, "choices": [{"name": "off", "display_name": "Off", "value": 0}, {"name": "bias_early", "display_name": "Bias Early", "value": 1}, {"name": "guarantee_early", "display_name": "Guarantee Early", "value": 2}]}, {"name": "black_panther_bias", "display_name": "Black Panther Bias", "description": "No effect when Item Smoothing is off.\n\nWhen Item Smoothing is on:\n   On: bias Black Panther (dash) to show up early: ~80% of seeds place it in\n      roughly the first half of the run (by seed/sphere ordering); the rest leave it to normal\n      placement.\n   Off: Black Panther places like any other progression item.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Toggle", "default": true}], "collapsed": false}, {"name": "Logic Difficulty", "options": [{"name": "logic_difficulty_preset", "display_name": "Logic Difficulty Preset", "description": "How much execution skill the logic may expect, beyond having the right souls.\nEach tier includes the ones below it.\n\n- canonical: developer-intended routes only.\n- standard: may expect kickable-enemy launches.\n- advanced: may also expect platform clips.\n- expert: may also expect pixel-perfect platforming.\n\nQuick-save resets are never expected; see Quick-Save Reset Logic.\nEach technique can be forced in or out of logic with its own option.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Choice", "default": 0, "choices": [{"name": "canonical", "display_name": "Canonical", "value": 0}, {"name": "standard", "display_name": "Standard", "value": 1}, {"name": "advanced", "display_name": "Advanced", "value": 2}, {"name": "expert", "display_name": "Expert", "value": 3}]}, {"name": "kickable_enemy_logic", "display_name": "Kickable-Enemy Logic", "description": "Whether logic may require launching off a kickable enemy.\ninherit: in logic from Standard difficulty up.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Choice", "default": 0, "choices": [{"name": "inherit", "display_name": "Inherit", "value": 0}, {"name": "in_logic", "display_name": "In Logic", "value": 1}, {"name": "out_of_logic", "display_name": "Out Of Logic", "value": 2}]}, {"name": "platform_clip_logic", "display_name": "Platform Clip Logic", "description": "Whether logic may require clipping the edge of platforms.\ninherit: in logic from Advanced difficulty up.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Choice", "default": 0, "choices": [{"name": "inherit", "display_name": "Inherit", "value": 0}, {"name": "in_logic", "display_name": "In Logic", "value": 1}, {"name": "out_of_logic", "display_name": "Out Of Logic", "value": 2}]}, {"name": "pixel_perfect_logic", "display_name": "Pixel-Perfect Logic", "description": "Whether logic may require pixel-perfect platforming.\ninherit: in logic at Expert difficulty.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Choice", "default": 0, "choices": [{"name": "inherit", "display_name": "Inherit", "value": 0}, {"name": "in_logic", "display_name": "In Logic", "value": 1}, {"name": "out_of_logic", "display_name": "Out Of Logic", "value": 2}]}, {"name": "quick_save_reset_logic", "display_name": "Quick-Save Reset Logic", "description": "Whether logic may require a quick save + reset, which respawns Soma at the room\nentrance. No difficulty expects this; it is in logic only if set to in_logic.", "randomizable": true, "visibility": 15, "type": "Choice", "default": 0, "choices": [{"name": "inherit", "display_name": "Inherit", "value": 0}, {"name": "in_logic", "display_name": "In Logic", "value": 1}, {"name": "out_of_logic", "display_name": "Out Of Logic", "value": 2}]}], "collapsed": false}, {"name": "Item & Location Options", "options": [{"name": "local_items", "display_name": "Local Items", "description": "Forces these items to be in their native world.", "randomizable": false, "visibility": 15, "type": "OptionSet", "default": [], "options": ["Lucky Charm", "Vjaya", "Cestus", "Short Sword", "Cape", "Grave Keeper", "Lance", "Mind Up (A)", "Potion (A)", "Potion (B)", "Leather Plate", "Flying Arm